WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.530
- Hey legal eagles.

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:04.340
Law school starts in August,
so you know what that means.

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:07.080
Time to get a new backpack!

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:10.010
Every law student needs a
backpack, it's unavoidable,

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.530
but there are lots of options out there,

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:13.920
and law school has a really
particular requirement

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.640
for what makes for a good or bad backpack.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:17.790
So today we're gonna discuss

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:19.210
what I think the best options are

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:21.640
for a backpack or bag in law school.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:22.510
By the end of this video,

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:25.150
you'll know exactly what
law school backpack to buy.

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:26.450
So stick around.

00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:29.033
(bright music)

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:33.920
Law school is probably
the last time in your life

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:36.780
that a backpack is a
mandatory requirement.

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:39.370
It's also probably the last
time that wearing a backpack

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:41.830
at all times is socially acceptable.

00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:44.420
I don't really know why,
they're really functional.

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:46.500
So here are a few reasons
why you should get

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:50.280
a good, sturdy backpack or
messenger bag in law school.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:52.730
Number one, you're most
likely going to be carrying

00:00:52.730 --> 00:00:55.150
your casebooks to and from class.

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:56.710
Even if you don't use them in class,

00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:59.130
which most people don't,
you might wanna read them

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:02.640
in the library before or after
class for homework purposes.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:07.277
This is a casebook,
they are big and heavy,

00:01:07.277 --> 00:01:11.360
and they're really bulky, so
you need a heavy-duty backpack

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:14.100
that is capable of
carrying multiple casebooks

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:15.680
without crushing your back.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:18.970
Now, number two, you're gonna
be taking your laptop with you

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:23.920
24/7, laptops are for law
students what water is to a fish.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:27.060
You would die without
it, so you're going to

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:29.660
use your laptop to take notes in class,

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:32.560
to write your outlines, and
most importantly when you go

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:35.280
on social media when you
need a break from law school.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:38.700
Now, you won't go anywhere
without your laptop,

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:41.311
so your backpack needs
to have a dedicated space

00:01:41.311 --> 00:01:44.500
to hold and protect your laptop.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:47.640
Now number three, you're
probably going to have all manner

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:52.122
of electronic doodads like
chargers and mice and cords,

00:01:52.122 --> 00:01:55.470
and writing implements
like pens and pencils

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:58.180
and highlighters, and additionally
you're probably going to

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:01.590
have a few snacks and caffeinated
liquids in your backpack.

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:02.610
So you need to have a way

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:05.190
to organize all of that stuff together.

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:08.630
So without further ado, here
are my main requirements

00:02:08.630 --> 00:02:10.540
for a law school backpack or bag.

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:13.190
Number one: it must be big,
it has to be big enough

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:15.330
to carry at least two casebooks.

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:18.250
Number two: it has to be
able to carry your laptop

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:21.050
and protect it so you don't destroy it.

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:24.150
Number three: your backpack
must be durable so it holds up

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:26.197
for at least one year and preferably,

00:02:26.197 --> 00:02:28.770
all three years in law school.

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:32.810
So generally there are three
types of backpacks or bags

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:35.460
that law students use in law school.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:38.270
Number one: there is the
regular old backpack.

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:41.640
It's got two straps, it's
got a flap at the top.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:43.670
It might have some zippers,
but this is the backpack

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:46.360
that you think of when
you think of a backpack.

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:49.020
Number two is the messenger bag

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:52.032
or something that looks
like a really big purse.

00:02:52.032 --> 00:02:55.510
These are the ones that generally
have one shoulder strap.

00:02:55.510 --> 00:02:58.930
You sling it over, and it's
generally one big pocket

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:02.303
with a flap over it and then
number three is the rollie bag.

00:03:02.303 --> 00:03:05.700
It's sort of a hybrid between a backpack

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:09.370
and the rolling suitcases
that you see at an airport.

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:12.300
Those are the three
main types of backpacks

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.280
that you see on a law school campus.

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:15.256
Let's talk about the
first category of options.

00:03:15.256 --> 00:03:18.930
This is the traditional backpack

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:21.800
On law school campuses,
you'll see a couple of brands

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:23.030
more often than not.

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:25.670
The first brand is Swiss Gear.

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:29.380
Here are a couple examples
of a Swiss Gear backpack.

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:32.960
They've got the red square with the white

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:35.680
or silver plus sign in the middle of it,

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:38.220
not unlike what you see
on a Swiss army knife.

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:40.179
I had a Swiss Gear backpack

00:03:40.179 --> 00:03:44.140
throughout my enter career
in college in undergrad.

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:46.050
I loved it, that thing was a tank,

00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:48.000
and it held up beautifully.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.625
These things are generally
cheap, they're pretty durable.

00:03:50.625 --> 00:03:53.630
They're not the most
fashion-forward option,

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:56.170
but I can personally vouch
that my personal Swiss Gear

00:03:56.170 --> 00:04:01.170
backpack lasted for years,
possibly even though high school,

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:02.450
now that I think about it.

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:05.029
But for me, when I got to
law school, a chest strap

00:04:05.029 --> 00:04:08.182
that went across my chest was a must.

00:04:08.182 --> 00:04:10.706
I find that it does a
really good job of helping

00:04:10.706 --> 00:04:14.010
shoulder the burden,
take some of the weight

00:04:14.010 --> 00:04:16.097
off of my shoulders and
put it on to my chest.

00:04:16.097 --> 00:04:19.551
You'll see these a lot
on hiking backpacks.

00:04:19.551 --> 00:04:22.270
So I upgraded to an OGIO backpack.

00:04:22.270 --> 00:04:26.283
This is my OGIO backpack,
this is an OGIO Gambit.

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:30.050
It's big enough to hold a 17-inch laptop.

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:33.910
It's got a separate pocket for a laptop.

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:36.000
It's got pockets all over the place.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.998
It easily holds multiple
electronic devices,

00:04:38.998 --> 00:04:42.340
and it seems to be as well built

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:46.580
as the Swiss Gear option that
I had throughout undergrad.

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:48.760
And most importantly,
it has a chest strap,

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:51.530
so that it can help shoulder the weight

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:53.120
of all the casebooks that I had.

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:55.390
The OGIO is a little bit more expensive,

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:58.390
but I found it to be
invaluable in law school

00:04:58.390 --> 00:05:00.400
and even after, I still have it.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:03.560
Another option is the Herschel backpack.

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:05.690
These are very popular right now.

00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:07.160
They are the more fashionable

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:09.700
of the traditional backpack options.

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:13.180
This a Herschel backpack that
I borrowed from a friend.

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:15.363
You can see it's got a
traditional top flap.

00:05:15.363 --> 00:05:19.561
It's got little leather
straps in the front,

00:05:19.561 --> 00:05:22.330
but it mainly consists of one large pocket

00:05:22.330 --> 00:05:26.090
with a laptop holder and then
a smaller pocket up front.

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:30.470
So you are paying for some
of that fashionableness

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:33.913
with less of the organizational features,

00:05:33.913 --> 00:05:37.310
but my friend bought one, it held up great

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:39.300
until one of the front straps broke,

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:41.900
but Herschel had a great
replacement policy,

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:44.930
and they sent a new bag within a week,

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:47.207
so I can say that the warranty is good,

00:05:47.207 --> 00:05:49.660
and the second one has
held up beautifully.

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:51.650
By the way, you can find links to all

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:53.900
of the backpacks and bags
that I'm discussing today

00:05:53.900 --> 00:05:57.650
down in the description below
that will take you directly

00:05:57.650 --> 00:06:00.000
to the Amazon link for the product.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:03.450
So finally in the traditional
backpack category,

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:05.820
you have brands like REI and Burton.

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:07.380
I've never earned one of those myself,

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:10.540
but they are very popular on
law school campuses right now.

00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:12.210
And based on the reviews that I've read,

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:14.950
they also sound like they
make really good options

00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:16.690
for law school backpacks as well.

00:06:16.690 --> 00:06:17.890
So I'll leave some links

00:06:17.890 --> 00:06:21.420
to those particular backpacks
in the description below.

00:06:21.420 --> 00:06:24.850
Okay, so that takes me
to the second category

00:06:24.850 --> 00:06:28.010
of backpack or bag that
you see in law school,

00:06:28.010 --> 00:06:30.310
and that is the messenger bag.

00:06:30.310 --> 00:06:32.510
Some people just cannot bring themselves

00:06:32.510 --> 00:06:36.841
to use a traditional
backpack, frankly, I get it.

00:06:36.841 --> 00:06:41.330
Backpacks form is really
not as good as its function,

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:44.660
and they are not the most
fashionable things to wear around.

00:06:44.660 --> 00:06:47.840
So for my friends that went
the non-backpack route,

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:50.080
most of them went with a messenger bag,

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:52.240
and particularly, a messenger bag

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:53.793
from a company called Timbuk2.

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:57.770
Here's a couple of examples
of those messenger bags.

00:06:57.770 --> 00:07:00.190
I can tell you from personal experience

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:03.120
that my friends who used
these messenger bags

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:05.930
were able to use them for multiple years.

00:07:05.930 --> 00:07:07.110
They held up beautifully,

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:09.790
and they fit a surprising
amount of weight.

00:07:09.790 --> 00:07:11.240
The only downside is that generally

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:15.240
you're using these as a
one-strap messenger bag,

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:17.010
and so all of the weight of your casebooks

00:07:17.010 --> 00:07:20.960
is gonna be shouldered on one shoulder.

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:24.710
So from what I saw, my friends
who had these messenger bags

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:26.220
were very happy with them.

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:29.320
They seem to be spacious enough
for casebooks and laptops,

00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:32.870
and most of them had
dedicated pockets for laptops,

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:35.130
and they appeared to be very durable.

00:07:35.130 --> 00:07:37.060
And most importantly, these messenger bags

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:40.136
were very, very high-quality polyester.

00:07:40.136 --> 00:07:43.420
Unfortunately, I can't
recommend any messenger bag

00:07:43.420 --> 00:07:46.480
that's made of leather or any
purse that's made of leather.

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:49.510
There's no doubt that
leather messenger bags

00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:52.700
and attache cases and purses look amazing,

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:55.489
but I have never seen a leather bag

00:07:55.489 --> 00:08:00.100
that was durable enough
to survive law school.

00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:04.390
So I can recommend the bags from Timbuk2,

00:08:04.390 --> 00:08:06.530
but I can't recommend, unfortunately,

00:08:06.530 --> 00:08:08.700
any leather messenger bags.

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:10.920
So that brings me to the third category

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:15.620
of bags and backpacks, and that
is the infamous rollie bag.

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:20.010
So, if the messenger bag is
the really fashionable option,

00:08:20.010 --> 00:08:23.360
the traditional backpack is
the sort of middle option,

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:26.030
well, then, rollie bags are
gonna be on the other end

00:08:26.030 --> 00:08:27.790
of the spectrum and those are for people

00:08:27.790 --> 00:08:30.840
who just don't care what they look like,

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:34.360
and want the absolute
most comfortable option.

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:36.190
That's what rollie bags do.

00:08:36.190 --> 00:08:39.270
These are bags that are sort of a hybrid

00:08:39.270 --> 00:08:41.410
between rolling luggage
that you see at airports

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:44.750
where you just kinda roll
it along on its wheels,

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:47.160
but as sort of an afterthought,
they have some straps

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:49.500
like a traditional backpack.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:52.421
Rollie bags are pervasive in law school,

00:08:52.421 --> 00:08:55.310
so don't be afraid of looking like a dork

00:08:55.310 --> 00:08:57.960
if you decide to choose a rollie bag.

00:08:57.960 --> 00:08:59.660
There's nothing wrong with it,

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:00.870
no one's gonna look down on you.

00:09:00.870 --> 00:09:04.270
People understand that
casebooks are really heavy,

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:06.220
laptops are heavy, all of the junk

00:09:06.220 --> 00:09:08.450
that you're gonna have in
your backpack is really heavy,

00:09:08.450 --> 00:09:11.129
so it's perfectly acceptable
to use a rollie bag

00:09:11.129 --> 00:09:13.090
when you get to law school.

00:09:13.090 --> 00:09:14.330
There will be lots of people

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:17.410
who likewise value function over form,

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:19.590
and buy a rollie bag for their stuff.

00:09:19.590 --> 00:09:20.810
There's sort of two options

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:23.210
when you're talking about rollie bags.

00:09:23.210 --> 00:09:26.500
First is what I would
say that most lawyers use

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:28.210
when they actually go to court.

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:31.820
These are generally referred
to as document bags.

00:09:31.820 --> 00:09:34.320
They have one large central area

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:36.780
where you can hold reams
and reams of paper,

00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:38.990
or in the case of a law student,

00:09:38.990 --> 00:09:41.270
their casebooks and their laptop.

00:09:41.270 --> 00:09:45.210
It's got lots of space but
there's sort of no frills,

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:47.940
and they are meant to get lots of paper

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:50.370
from one area to the other.

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:52.800
If you are dead set on saving money

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:55.420
and want to buy the
thing that you're going

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:57.360
to use most likely in practice,

00:09:57.360 --> 00:10:01.200
the document bag like this
one is probably your best bet.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:03.780
That is what lawyers bring into court

00:10:03.780 --> 00:10:06.060
when they graduate from law school.

00:10:06.060 --> 00:10:09.480
Alternatively, you can get a
hybrid backpack with wheels.

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:13.970
For example, this one from
High Sierra has wheels

00:10:13.970 --> 00:10:17.500
on the bottom but also straps
like a traditional backpack.

00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:20.080
This is probably what you'll
see more of in law school.

00:10:20.080 --> 00:10:23.640
Something that is so sort
of like a real backpack,

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:25.910
but has some wheels built
into it so that you can

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:28.970
carry it like a backpack
when you're walking

00:10:28.970 --> 00:10:31.865
over dirt or grass, but
you can use the wheels

00:10:31.865 --> 00:10:34.370
when you are walking over concrete.

00:10:34.370 --> 00:10:36.800
So those are the main
options when you're talking

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:40.240
about backpacks, bags, and rollie bags.

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:41.960
There is no one right answer,

00:10:41.960 --> 00:10:43.670
you have to choose for yourself.

00:10:43.670 --> 00:10:45.710
You'll see that law students are split

00:10:45.710 --> 00:10:48.060
roughly a third for each category.

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:50.550
So whatever route you choose,

00:10:50.550 --> 00:10:52.610
there will be other students like you

00:10:52.610 --> 00:10:54.352
who made similar decisions, and frankly,

00:10:54.352 --> 00:10:57.130
you really can't go
wrong, so get the backpack

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:58.640
or bag that works for you

00:10:58.640 --> 00:11:00.700
so that's one less thing
you have to worry about

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:03.000
for when you start law school in the fall.

